    <briefdescription>
<para>Returns three numbers which are the global sum of a variable. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns three numbers which are the global sum of a variable (1) on its home model grid, (2) after interpolation to the other side grid(s), and (3) after re_interpolation back onto its home side grid(s). Conservation_check must be called by all PEs to work properly.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>d</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>real(r8_kind) data </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>grid_id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>3 character grid ID </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">xmap</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>exchange grid </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">global</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>sum of a variable on home model grid, after side grid interpolation and after reinterpolation</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<linebreak/>
Example usage: <programlisting filename=".F90"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">call<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">conservation_check(d,<sp/>grid_id,<sp/>xmap,remap_order)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
